      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The remark says “a recorded CHSH functional outside the bound of a declared representable model would exclude that model class” under the stated detection and selection assumptions. A finite recorded CHSH value can exceed 2 with positive probability under a local-response model: take $\\lambda=(A_0,A_1,B_0,B_1)$ uniformly distributed on $\\{-1,+1\\}^4$, with deterministic coordinate responses. Each pair table is uniform and the true CHSH value is $0$. With one independent sample per setting pair, the product-sign sequence $(+1,+1,+1,-1)$ has probability $1/16$ and gives sample CHSH $4$. Thus a finite-sample violation alone does not exclude the local-response class; a qualified statistical inference is needed.",
